      "writtenOn": "2022-03-13T23:57:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there was a doc, but what I recall from review comments was that if a particular configuration may need to handle something specially, the subsystem should provide hooks to register those functions and can provide a default implementation that runs if no hooks are configured on a given extension point.\n\nI don\u0027t think we want to do this right now, since:\n* We currently only need to support this one board\n* Requiring users to define symbols with magic names doesn\u0027t match Zephyr coding style\n* Cleaning it up to be an actual subsystem will allow hooks for extension points to be more naturally added\n\nThis adds complexity (as you note) for something that will be improved by other future work and would itself need to be cleaned up as well.",
      "parentUuid": "ce28a478_2d0aac93",
      "revId": "423e8d1ec218cee3d6892815cd93c918e4f51297",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61ce08c3_e2898892",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
